A||N||5||Verticalspeed||**Something Is Wrong With My Balls -Joints**||||5||
Z||000000||Verticalspeed||02-03-2001||12:41 PM||||I have had my car aligned yesterday. Tires balanced, all 4. Rear end has new ball joints. Struts and shocks are new. Here's the problem. at highway speeds 65-75MPH the front end shakes as if a wheel was slightly loose. I can't tell if it is coming from the right or left front side. But the wheel seems to wobble and the interior vibrates or even shakes!!! It's scary! Tires are new.<BR>I am wondering if the balls joints are shock, the steering rack bushing or tie rod ends. IF you had this same problem, how did you fix it. It almost feels like the wheel will spin off the car and I can't go much faster than 60-65 without the re-ocurring problem. HELP! Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Verticalspeed||02-03-2001||12:45 PM||||Correction: This was ocurring BEFORE the alignment too. So I had the tires checked, balanced as well. I don't have a bouncy front end just a vibration and wobble on the front wheel(s). I am checking the axle nuts||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||02-03-2001||01:03 PM||||sounds like a F____d up alignment job. A good wheel man would have found any bad joints. Would have had a goood hard look at all the bushings as well.<P>Is the car still full stock? What year? Did you get a printout of the alignment? I won't ever use a shop that won't give me the printouts from before and after. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phaeton||02-03-2001||01:05 PM||||The alignment shop should have checked all the ball joints for wear before performing the alignment.  Standard practice to avoid problems like this where the alignment doesn't "take". <BR>Check the joints and if any are bad have the same shop replace them and a realignment should be done at no cost.<BR>Is there more play in the steering wheel when straight than when turned almost to full lock?  If so then this could be worn rack.  No cheap fix for that.||||reg||12
Z||000004||Verticalspeed||02-03-2001||04:01 PM||||  Hi...I have a vibration on the front end (a shake too) between 65-75 MPH<BR>that's almost scary. I did the 9 to 3 test and there is about 1/8" play or less on the front right wheel. I haven't checked the left yet.<BR>The 12 to 6 test is solid. No play. So I think the ball joints are fine.<BR>In examining things a bit closer, I think the only possibility of slack is in the outter tie rod ends. I have checked for play in the steering rack and it seems o.k. Before I buy the parts, I wondered if you would agree with me on this assumption. I don't know how to check the tie rod end itself but I can move it around semi-easily. I don't know how solid tthe shaft needs to be after being greased. How do you tell if A TIE ROD  end is bad?<BR>The car tracks better after the alignment which is under a 90 day warranty.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||02-03-2001||07:08 PM||||Have all wheels and tires re-balanced and have it re-aligned. Sounds like a crappy job was performed. Might want to consider a different place.<P>Tie-rod ends, if there is slack, they're bad.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 02-03-2001).]||||reg||1
